  "findings": [
    "Existing from_view matches native std::string_view constructor by stopping at first NUL. No production change required.",
    "Native Copy(view), Copy(ptr,length), operator=(view), AssignCat(view), Cat(view), operator+(view), operator+=(view) retain embedded NUL bytes. Existing copy and generic slice operands match.",
    "From<&[u8]> is a full-span conversion used by generic append and Cat dispatch; routing it through from_view would regress those overloads. Explicit from_view is the native view constructor.",
    "Existing original declaration tests use no embedded NULs for the view methods; three new tests assert this behavior against ten native output rows."
  ],
